DKMS only: keep the symbol CRCs of the stock include/media/ipu-bridge.h

Patches 0002 and 0005 change struct ipu_sensor (the size of prop_names
and ep_properties), which the exported ipu_bridge_init() (through
ipu_parse_sensor_fwnode_t) and ipu_bridge_parse_ssdb() take a pointer to.
With CONFIG_MODVERSIONS the CRCs of these symbols then differ from the ones
the stock importers were built with (intel-ipu6, intel-ipu7, ipu3-cio2,
ivsc-csi, intel_cvs), and those modules refuse to load against the DKMS
ipu-bridge.ko.

The layout change is private to ipu-bridge: the structures are allocated
and filled inside it. Most importers pass ipu-bridge's own
ipu_bridge_parse_ssdb() as the callback; the one that brings its own
(atomisp) writes only fields in front of the changed ones (link, lanes,
mclkspeed, rotation, orientation, vcm_type), whose offsets do not move.
So the CRCs are computed from the stock layout (__GENKSYMS__ is defined
only while genksyms reads the source) and the module is compiled with the
new one. dkms/check-build.sh compares the resulting CRCs with the kernel's
Module.symvers; without this patch ipu_bridge_init and
ipu_bridge_parse_ssdb differ (measured on linux-surface 7.3.4-2).

Applied by dkms/gen.sh to the bundled copy of the header, only when this
repository's patches changed it.

--- a/include/media/ipu-bridge.h
+++ b/include/media/ipu-bridge.h
@@ -135,7 +135,9 @@
 	char data_lanes[11];
 	char remote_endpoint[16];
 	char link_frequencies[17];
+#ifndef __GENKSYMS__
 	char clock_noncontinuous[20];
+#endif
 };
 
 struct ipu_node_names {
@@ -178,7 +180,11 @@
 	const char *vcm_type;
 
 	struct ipu_property_names prop_names;
+#ifdef __GENKSYMS__
+	struct property_entry ep_properties[5];
+#else
 	struct property_entry ep_properties[IPU_BRIDGE_EP_NUM_ENTRIES];
+#endif
 	struct property_entry dev_properties[5];
 	struct property_entry ipu_properties[3];
 	struct property_entry ivsc_properties[1];
